meta {
  name: suggest a session title
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/sessions/{{sessionId}}/title/suggest
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Ask the session's recorded provider and model once for a title of three to five words from its first prompt (thinking off, 30 s limit). A session with a hand-set title is not sent. 200 {title?, titleSource?, pinned, suggested}, suggested false when no title came; 400 malformed id, 404 fenced out or session not stored.
  
  CAUTION: This spends one model call on the provider the session recorded, and sends it the session's first prompt.
  
  Fence: host+origin — Loopback fence plus Origin check: an Origin header, if present, must be loopback. REST clients send no Origin header, which counts as safe — requests pass. A manually added foreign Origin answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: yes
}
